papers.abstract:
For a finite dimensional semisimple Lie algebra $\mathfrak{g}$, the multiplicity $c_{\lambda\mu}^{
u}$ of an irreducible $V(
u),$ inside the tensor product $V(\lambda)\otimes V(\mu),$ of two highest weight irreducible representations can be realised as the dimension of the Kostant--Parthasarathy--Ranga Rao--Varadarajan multiplicity space inside $V(\lambda)$, $V(\mu)$ or $V(
u)$. A result of Panyushev and Yakimova shows how to split the multiplicity space for $c_{\lambda\lambda}^{
u}$ inside $V(
u)$ into symmetric and alternating parts when $V(\lambda)$ is self-dual. For finite-dimensional semisimple or symmetric Kac--Moody, we extend this to Kostant--Kumar modules $K(\lambda,w,\lambda)=\mathfrak{Ug}(v_\lambda\otimes v_{w\lambda})$ when $w=w^{-1},$ and for all dominant weights $\lambda.$ We show that the multiplicities of an irreducible in the symmetric and alternating parts of $K(\lambda,w,\lambda)$ are given by the dimensions of the eigenspaces of the Tits lift $\widetilde w$ of $w$ on the multiplicity space corresponding to eigenvalues $\pm 1$. This recovers the result for the full tensor product by letting $w=w_0,$ the longest element of the Weyl group. In type A, we also discuss connections to a combinatorial interpretation due to Carr'e and Leclerc in terms of domino tableaux.
